1
00:00:00,047 --> 00:00:04,583
The duty matrix: employees × days of the month. Red dates are understaffed.

2
00:00:04,583 --> 00:00:15,982
Auto-generation creates a new draft and fills it, respecting rest, duty limits and synergies.

3
00:00:15,982 --> 00:00:20,973
The draft opens in its own tab. The approved schedule does not change.

4
00:00:20,973 --> 00:00:25,046
Hover an event to see required (red) and preferred (yellow) rest days.

5
00:00:25,046 --> 00:00:37,593
Click any cell to assign an event. The rules are checked right away.

6
00:00:37,593 --> 00:00:43,986
Hide employees you do not need right now…

7
00:00:43,986 --> 00:00:47,754
…and bring them all back with one click.

8
00:00:47,754 --> 00:00:54,364
The Statistics column shows each employee’s days per event type.

9
00:00:54,364 --> 00:01:11,479
Approving the draft makes it the schedule of the month.

10
00:01:11,479 --> 00:01:27,735
A period can count only some days of the week, e.g. weekends of every month.

11
00:01:27,735 --> 00:01:33,857
Duty limits cap duty days per period, as a hard rule or a warning.

12
00:01:33,857 --> 00:01:46,798
Reports show workload distribution and staffing deficits.
